      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Given that  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-7{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{4}\\in R\\}$, find a basis for $\\text{Null}(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "Any vector in $\\text{Null}(A)$ has the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{4}\\in R.\n$$\n\nExpanding, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, a basis for $\\text{Null}(A)$ is\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nsince it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$",
